## 14. KNOWN LIMITS & BACKLOG

### Working, deployed

- Multi-tenant DB
- 4 roles with correct guards
- Marketplace matching (interest-based)
- Wellness check-ins (worker + client)
- Coordinator roster with real-time status
- Verification queue with dual-worker context labels
- Admin control tower (KPIs, charts, alerts, activity)
- Register: 3 doors, funding fields, worker preselection
- Mobile responsive
- Session-expiry guards on every page
- **Worker onboarding flow** — `/onboarding` + `POST /api/worker-onboarding`; login redirects incomplete workers
- **Worker tab switcher** — dual workers see Marketplace + Roster tabs
- **Email verification** — token table, `/api/verify-email/:token`, resend endpoint, `/verify-email` page
- **Password reset** — `/api/auth/forgot-password` + `/api/auth/reset-password` + UI pages
- **Real password hashing** — bcrypt (`$2…`), legacy plaintext tolerated at login for seed accounts
- **Login rate limiting** — 5 failures / 15 min window
- **Bearer JWT auth** — `signToken` / `verifyToken`; `x-user-id` header still supported as legacy

### Missing / post-pilot

| Feature | Notes |
|---|---|
| MFA | Evgeny's requirement for all logins |
| MS365 SSO | Entra ID for staff |
| Real email sending (prod) | Resend configured but restricted to own address until domain is verified |
| Payment gateway | Stripe via VisualCare integration |
| Progress notes | Legal evidence, mandatory per meetings |
| Funding display in coordinator view | Schema has it, UI doesn't |
| VisualCare API integration | Schema + sync log exist, no live calls |
| Azure Postgres migration | Post-pilot target |
| Roster caching layer | Currently 3 queries per page — could be 1 |

### Cosmetic / housekeeping

- `src/dist/` and `src/functions/` tracked in git (should be gitignored)
- Old "helphome" casing in `<title>` of index.html
- Alert dismissal is client-side only (returns on refresh — by design)
- **Dev-only endpoints to remove before public launch:** `GET /api/_test/db/counts`, `POST /api/_test/cleanup`, `POST /api/_test/complete-onboarding`
- **Audit future migrations** for unexpected `DROP COLUMN` lines (see §12.3)

---

## 15. EMERGENCY RECOVERY

### Worker broken → rollback

```
Cloudflare dashboard
→ Workers & Pages → helphome-api → Deployments
→ click previous working version → Rollback
```

Effective within 30 seconds.

### Pages broken → rollback

```
Cloudflare dashboard
→ Workers & Pages → helphome-app → Deployments
→ click previous working version → Rollback
```

### Supabase connection issues

- Free tier has automatic daily backups (00:00 UTC)
- Restore via Supabase dashboard → Database → Backups
- If password leaked: rotate in Supabase → update `.dev.vars` and Worker secret

### Local PGlite corrupted

**NEVER use `taskkill /F /IM node.exe` — corrupts PGlite.**

If corrupted:

```bash
# Stop backend with Ctrl+C
mv .data/pg .data/pg.corrupted
mkdir -p .data/pg
# restart backend — seeds fresh
```

### Git rollback

```bash
git log --oneline -20         # find good commit hash
git revert <hash>             # safe undo (new commit)
git push origin feature/multitenant
```

### Full local reset

```bash
# Stop both servers
rm -rf .data/pg && mkdir -p .data/pg
npx tsx -e "import { getDb } from './src/db/connection.ts'; getDb().then(() => { console.log('DB OK'); process.exit(0); })"
```

